---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/data';
// The copyright holder is the Owner name from site.config.json (set on the Settings page); the build refuses to finish without it.
const holder = site.feed.owner_name;
const year = new Date(site.launch).getUTCFullYear();
---
<Base title="Credits and Permissions | An Anglican Synaxarium" description="Sources, permissions and attributions for the audio, liturgical texts and images used by An Anglican Synaxarium." path="/credits/">
  <main class="entry-wrap" style="flex:1">
    <article class="entry-card about credits-page">
      <h1 class="entry-title">Credits and Permissions</h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p><em>An Anglican Synaxarium</em> is a non-commercial project of Christian education, devotion, and spiritual formation. Its hagiographical entries are original compositions unless otherwise noted. Certain audio, liturgical texts, and images are used from other sources under their respective permissions, licenses, or copyright provisions.</p>

        <h2>Licence</h2>
        <h3>Text</h3>
        <p>The written entries on this site are © {year} {holder} and are licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/" rel="noopener">Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)</a>. You may copy, print and share them, and adapt them (for example, translate them or adapt them for your parish), for non-commercial purposes, provided that you credit {holder} and <em>An Anglican Synaxarium</em>, say what you changed, and share any adaptation under the same licence.</p>
        <p>This licence does not cover the audio recordings; the collects and liturgical texts taken from published sources, credited below; the images and the Compass Rose emblem; or the BBC bell.</p>
        <h3>Recordings</h3>
        <p>The podcast recordings are © {year} {holder}. All rights reserved. You are welcome to listen and subscribe in any podcast app; please do not copy or republish the recordings without permission. The opening bell is © BBC and is used under the licence described below.</p>

        <h2>Audio</h2>
        <p>The podcast opens with a bell from the BBC Sound Effects Library.</p>
        <dl class="credit-block">
          <dt>Title / Description</dt><dd>Bell, Church: Catholic Church Bells, Sanctus Bell</dd>
          <dt>Filename</dt><dd>BellsCatholic.BBC.EC91Db.wav</dd>
          <dt>Sound ID</dt><dd>28593</dd>
          <dt>Library</dt><dd>BBC Sound Effects Library</dd>
          <dt>Manufacturer</dt><dd>BBC</dd>
          <dt>Copyright</dt><dd>© 2026 BBC. All Rights Reserved.</dd>
        </dl>
        <p>The sound is distributed through AvoSound and is used under the <a href="https://github.com/bbcarchdev/Remarc/blob/master/doc/2016.09.27_RemArc_Content_licence_Terms_of_Use_final.pdf" rel="noopener">BBC Content Licence for RemArc</a> for a personal, non-commercial project.</p>
        <p class="credit-line">bbc.co.uk — © 2026 BBC</p>
        <p>The BBC does not endorse, sponsor, or otherwise approve <em>An Anglican Synaxarium</em>.</p>

        <h2>Collects and Liturgical Texts</h2>
        <p>Some collects and other liturgical texts used in <em>An Anglican Synaxarium</em> come from authorized Anglican liturgical sources. Other prayers are newly composed for the project.</p>

        <h3>The Book of Common Prayer</h3>
        <p class="citation"><em>The Book of Common Prayer and Administration of the Sacraments and Other Rites and Ceremonies of the Church, according to the use of The Episcopal Church.</em> 1979. Published by Church Publishing Incorporated.</p>

        <h3>Lesser Feasts and Fasts 2024</h3>
        <p class="citation"><em>Lesser Feasts and Fasts 2024</em>, conforming to The General Convention 2024. Published by Church Publishing Incorporated.</p>
        <p class="citation">Copyright © 2024 by The Domestic and Foreign Missionary Society of The Protestant Episcopal Church in the United States of America.</p>
        <p>The book states: “Portions of this book may be reproduced by a congregation for its own use. Commercial or large-scale reproduction, or reproduction for sale, of any portion of this book or of the book as a whole, without the written permission of Church Publishing Incorporated is prohibited.”</p>

        <h3>Newly Composed Collects</h3>
        <p>Collects identified as newly composed are original to <em>An Anglican Synaxarium</em>. The collects in the Synaxarium do not all come from <em>Lesser Feasts and Fasts</em>: the project uses received collects, adapted prayers where authorized and appropriate, and newly composed prayers, according to its editorial rules.</p>

        <h2>Images</h2>
        <h3>Background photograph</h3>
        <p>The stained-glass background on the home page is a detail of the west window of Canterbury Cathedral, cropped, resized, and lightened.</p>
        <dl class="credit-block">
          <dt>Photograph</dt><dd>Stained glass in west window, Canterbury Cathedral</dd>
          <dt>Photographer</dt><dd>Jules &amp; Jenny from Lincoln, UK</dd>
          <dt>Date</dt><dd>2 February 2014</dd>
          <dt>Source</dt><dd><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stained_glass_in_west_window,_Canterbury_Cathedral.jpg" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></dd>
          <dt>License</dt><dd><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/" rel="noopener">Creative Commons Attribution 2.0 Generic (CC BY 2.0)</a></dd>
          <dt>Changes</dt><dd>Cropped, resized, and lightened under a veil of color.</dd>
        </dl>

        <h3>Podcast cover and header artwork</h3>
        <p>The cover art of <em>An Anglican Synaxarium</em> was designed for the project. It carries the Compass Rose, the emblem of the Anglican Communion.</p>

        <h2>About Rights and Attribution</h2>
        <p><em>An Anglican Synaxarium</em> is produced as a non-commercial work of Christian education, devotion, and spiritual formation. Attribution on this page identifies the sources of materials used by the project and does not imply endorsement by the BBC, Church Publishing Incorporated, museums, archives, churches, artists, or other credited institutions unless explicitly stated.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</Base>
